# Cursor Rules for StudentOps AI

## Environment & Tooling
- Always use `uv` for Python backend commands (`uv sync`, `uv run uvicorn ...`, `uv run pytest`).
- Never use raw `pip install` or direct `python` execution.
- Use `npm run build` in `frontend/` to verify TypeScript types after modifying frontend files.

## Code Standards
- **Backend (FastAPI)**:
  - Async SQLAlchemy (`AsyncSession`) and async endpoints throughout.
  - Model definitions in `app/models/entities.py` (SQLAlchemy) and `app/models/schemas.py` (Pydantic v2).
  - All agent interactions go through `app/agent/react_agent.py` and `app/agent/tools.py`.
  - Sensitive operations (mass messaging/reminders) must trigger human confirmation.
  - LLM calls use OpenRouter SSE streaming via `httpx.AsyncClient`.
  - Never hardcode secrets. Read strictly from `app.core.config.settings`.

- **Frontend (React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind)**:
  - Strict TypeScript typing matching `src/types/index.ts`.
  - Modern, award-winning SaaS visual standards (Linear/Stripe/Vercel light-mode aesthetic).
  - No AI-slop visual tropes (no neon cyberpunk glows or generic dark template cards).
  - No emojis in UI components, buttons, agent chat responses, or prompts. Use Lucide icons instead.
  - Streaming responses render token-by-token with SSE and cursor animation.
  - Maintain bilingual support (English + Arabic with `arabic_name` and `Cairo` font).

## Testing & Verification
- Unit tests: `cd backend && uv run pytest tests -v`
- Frontend build: `cd frontend && npm run build`
